Tanya —

For the PA workflow SLAs: could you collect what the plans are actually
telling providers about determination timelines on new specialty products?
Two things to keep separate in your notes: (1) the plan's quoted working
SLA, and (2) the statutory clock. The statute table Aaron compiled caps
standard determinations at seven calendar days with a 72-hour expedited
lane in most of the states that regulate it — Florida and Missouri allow
ten days and Tennessee fourteen — and applies to fully-insured and
Medicaid managed care lives (ERISA self-funded plans are exempt). That's
the floor the workflow enforces state by state, whatever a rep quotes on
the phone. Where you hear numbers longer than the applicable statute, flag
them: those become escalation triggers in the failure paths, and the field
team needs a script for them.

James

